comments.body:
LIN-4404 (Part 1) is merged and live on production (`ecabd3d76`, PR #2386), so this ticket is no longer blocked. What it can read:
- `readTaskCost` in `lib/task-cost-read.js`, which returns `lineagesTruncated` and per-lineage `incomplete`;
- `dispatches[].firstRequestAt` / `lastRequestAt`;
- the `foundedElsewhere` opt-in on `readCost`.

Lineages from before about 4 Nov 2026 have `dispatches: null`, because there are no request records for them. The timeline should show those as sessions without a span.

## Implementation: PR open, CI green

PR: https://github.com/JKershaw/LinearViewer/pull/2390 (commit `73d53614e`, branch `feat/lin-4405-sessions-on-one-clock`). CI `ci-success` passed: unit tests, all four E2E shards and the secret scan.

**What landed.** Every task page now has a "Sessions on one clock" section under Stages. It draws every session that ran the task on one clock, each with:
- its kind: held, fresh, or just its kind name;
- its model;
- elapsed versus worked time;
- its cost;
- wake and resume ticks.

It also shows the merge mark, or "merged, time not recorded". A session from before request records existed is drawn as an outline marked "working times unknown". Lineages founded on another task show only this task's dispatches, clipped to this task's clock and left out of the total.

It reads at 390px (labels above full-width tracks) and on desktop (a label column beside each track). Guests see the same picture with no dollars on `/t/:token`, `/t/:token/timeline` and `/t/:token/state`. The page repaints the section from a fragment, at most once per 60s window, and stops when the poll stops.

**Witnesses**
- The LIN-4393 fixture, taken from the real read: eight lanes. The autopilot was held 63 min and **worked 2m 22s**, measured, against the plan's estimate of about 6 min. It has five wake ticks. The build has two segments and a leftover resume tick. The two surveys run side by side, and there is a merge mark.
- Every case the slice lists has a test.
- Builder note 9 goes through the real store, the real cost read and the real page.
- The three guest responses carry no dollar and no cost attribute.
- The e2e test checks 390px and desktop.
- I broke each guarded behaviour once (15 targeted breaks). Each break turned its test red, and every file was restored afterwards.

**Departures**, with reasons, are posted on LIN-4395 (comment `d61b450d`):
- a shared 30s fragment cache replaces `cachedLoadPage`, which settles the open question about the cache;
- per-lineage `incomplete`, not the shared truncation flag, decides "not complete";
- a ci-wake resume does not make a lineage held;
- the outline is the representation for old lineages;
- the corrected worked-time figure;
- the app's own stage words in labels;
- the desktop grid area.

DECISION: no new cut to `## As asked`. The only cut is the one already ruled: guests see the picture without dollars. No BLOCKED.
